With --allow-unused, templates nothing executes are listed as a note and
do not fail the check: a project may render them outside muxt. A route
template with no generated handler still fails.

Command line: muxt check --allow-unused
-- config.json --
{
	"Verbose": false,
	"AllowUnused": true,
	"TemplatesVariables": [
		"templates"
	]
}
-- index.gohtml --
{{define "index"}}<h1>{{.Title}}</h1>{{end}}
{{define "orphan"}}<p>never rendered</p>{{end}}
{{define "GET /items Items()"}}{{template "row" .}}{{end}}
{{define "row"}}<tr></tr>{{end}}
-- server.go --
package server

import "io"

type Page struct {
	Title string
}

func RenderIndex(w io.Writer, page Page) error {
	return templates.ExecuteTemplate(w, "index", page)
}
-- want/checked.txt --
1
-- want/error.txt --
1 error
-- want/log.txt --
Route templates with no generated handler; run muxt generate to wire them up:
  - index.gohtml:3:32: "GET /items Items()"
Unused templates (allowed by --allow-unused):
  - index.gohtml:2:20: "orphan"
